            <ArticleTitle>First-Line Abemaciclib Effective in ER+ Breast Cancer.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>OF6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1158/2159-8290.CD-NB2017-135</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Interim data from the MONARCH3 study indicate that abemaciclib is an effective first-line therapy for advanced ER-positive, HER2-negative breast cancer. Adding the investigational CDK4/6 inhibitor to letrozole significantly improved patients' progression-free survival, compared with those given a placebo alongside endocrine therapy.</AbstractText>
